Records of the society are retained according to the retention rule stated in the statute. Specifically, records are kept for the period named in the schedule of the statute. The schedule specifies that ledgers are retained for eleven calendar years, after which they are shredded.[[cite:obs-effbdea19647ab40ea00f757bb9314b3e8a0956f "Records of the society are retained for the period named in the schedule of this statute."]][[cite:obs-0216270952671e075ed4eaa0eefd13f712469dbe "Ledgers: eleven calendar years, shredding afterwards."]]